window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"malphite","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Malphite","Malphite","Skill","Skill","Malphite","Malphite"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q at 3 lets you poke and shield off The Darkin Glaive chip"},{"when":"1st item","text":"Armor spike — but Aureate Rush burns percent health anyway"},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Grievous Wounds: his Q and R heal, and his passive revives"}],"wants":{"you":["Grievous Wounds before long trades","Granite Shield resets between glaive pokes","R only when his Q recast is down"],"foe":["Level-2 all-in before your Granite Shield","Gank setups off his ult","Extended trades where Q and R heal him"]},"early":"Play the first levels patient: level 1 is a pure farm split, and level 2 is his all-in before your armour ramps — concede ground, not health. The Darkin Glaive is an auto reset that heals him, so his wind-up is the cue to step back. At 3, Q pokes and shields the chip off.","mid":"Through 4-5 keep resetting Granite Shield between glaive pokes and force nothing. At 6, count the numbers rather than trusting the swing: Unstoppable Force is 130 seconds and his knock-ups are a 10-second Q recast and a 14-second Dreaded Return pull. You lose that race, so R answers a commit he has already made — it never opens.","late":"First item snaps the lane your way — armour does answer his physical damage. Two items is not unbreakable: Aureate Rush burns percent health armour cannot reduce, and Cultivation of War revives him. Buy Grievous Wounds against Q and R, and stop offering him side-lane duels.","whys":["Level 1 is an even farm start — neither of you has spiked yet, so just split the wave and trade last-hits.","Level 2 is his window — The Darkin Glaive resets his auto and heals him before your armour ramps, so concede the trade.","Level 3 evens — Seismic Shard pokes and shields off the glaive, but it costs 70 mana to his 25.","Levels 4-5 stay even as Granite Shield soaks the glaive — step out after each exchange so the shield recharges.","Level 6 is a skill-check — Unstoppable Force is 130s against a 10s Darkin Glaive recast and a 14s Dreaded Return pull, so your R answers his commit and never opens.","First item is your spike — armour and Ground Slam answer his physical damage, and trades stop being close.","Aureate Rush burns percent health and his passive revives him — armour alone does not win you the side lane."]});
